{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"With Candana, Etc.","html":"<article id='sn40.11'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 40.11 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 40.11 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>1. Moggallānavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>1. By Moggallāna </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Candanasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>With Candana, Etc. </span></h1></header>\n<p><span class='root'>Atha kho candano devaputto …pe…. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Then the godling Candana … </span></p>\n<p><span class='root'>Atha kho suyāmo devaputto …pe…. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the godling Suyāma … </span></p>\n<p><span class='root'>Atha kho santusito devaputto …pe…. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the godling Santusita … </span></p>\n<p><span class='root'>Atha kho sunimmito devaputto …pe…. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the godling Sunimmita … </span></p>\n<p><span class='root'>Atha kho vasavatti devaputto …pe…. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>the godling Vasavatti … </span></p>\n<p class='expansion-instructions'><span class='root'>(Yathā sakkasuttaṁ tathā ime pañca peyyālā vitthāretabbā.) </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>(Tell in full  as in the Discourse With Sakka.) </span></p>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Ekādasamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Moggallānavaggo paṭhamo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Savitakkāvitakkañca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>sukhena ca upekkhako; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ākāsañceva viññāṇaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>ākiñcaṁ nevasaññinā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Animitto ca sakko ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>candanekādasena cāti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endkanda'><span class='root'>Moggallānasaṁyuttaṁ samattaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Linked Discourses on Moggallāna are complete. </span></p></article>"}
